 "decision": {
  "basis": "E9 clears the encoder-latency screen (-23% P50) and its Chinese probes match L12, but its English (FLEURS) probe is 13-16% worse (CI excludes 0), the estimated end-to-end saving is only ~7-10% because the Reader is 52-68% of end-to-end time, and a frozen linear probe is not evidence about a retrained early-exit model. E6 fails the accuracy screen in every set. Not GO (language-specific regression; e2e saving below the screen); not NO-GO (a trained early-exit model was not tested).",
